{"type":"thinking","text":"Good, hack active. Now I need to analyze the table structure. Let me look again at the region.\n\nThe region 0x6700-0x6800 (prgRom). CPU = offset + 0x8000. So 0x6792 = CPU $E792.\n\nWait, that's in the enemy graphics area. Let me recall SMB disassembly: There is `EnemyGfxTable` at around $E7? Hmm, CPU $E700-$E800 region. Actually the SMB disassembly has `EnemyGraphicsTable` maybe at $E7A0? Let me not rely.\n\nLet me examine the exact structure. From the read at 0x6770:\n```\n0x6770: 8F 8E 8E 8F FC FC 95 94 94 95 FC FC DC DC DF DF\n0x678A: DC DC DD DD DE DE FC FC B2 B3 B4 B5 FC FC B6 B3 B7 B5\n0x67A2: FC FC 70 71 72 73 FC FC 6E 6E 6F 6F FC FC 6D 6D ...\n```\nWait I mis-indexed. Let me redo carefully. The read at 26480 = 0x6770, length 96, bytes:\n[143,142,142,143, 252,252,149,148,148,149, 252,252,220,220,223,223, 220,220,221,221, 222,222, 252,252, 178,179,180,181, 252,252,182,179,183,181, 252,252,112,113,114,115, 252,252,110,110,111,111, 252,252,109,109,111,111, 252,252,111,111,110,110, 252,252,111,111,109,109, 252,252,244,244,245,245, 252,252,244,244,245,245, 252,252,245,245,244,244, 252,252,245,245,244,244, 252,252,252,252,239,239, 185,184]\n\nIndex:\n0:143 (0x6770)\n1:142\n2:142\n3:143\n4:252\n5:252\n6:149\n7:148\n8:148\n9:149\n10:252\n11:252\n12:220\n13:220\n14:223\n15:223\n16:220\n17:220\n18:221\n19:221\n20:222\n21:222\n22:252\n23:252\n24:178\n25:179\n26:180\n27:181\n28:252\n29:252\n30:182\n31:179\n32:183\n33:181\n34:252\n35:252\n36:112\n37:113\n38:114\n39:115   <- 0x6770+36 = 0x6794... wait 0x6770 = 26480. 26480+36 = 26516. But search said 0x6794 = 26516. Yes! So 0x6794 holds 112 (0x70). And 0x6792 = 26514 holds 252 (index 34). Good.\n...\n36:112 (0x6794)\n37:113\n38:114\n39:115\n40:252\n41:252\n42:110\n43:110\n44:111\n45:111\n46:252\n47:252\n48:109\n49:109\n50:111\n51:111\n52:252\n53:252\n54:111\n55:111\n56:110\n57:110\n58:252\n59:252\n60:111\n61:111\n62:109\n63:109\n64:252\n65:252\n66:244\n67:244\n68:245\n69:245\n70:252\n71:252\n72: