econd, press Start again\"). So after reset we're on the title. Press Start once, wait, press Start again? The mapping's overworld reach used [{start,6},{none,60},{start,6},{none,60}]. But that's from the attract demo? Actually mapping says from title or attract: press Start, wait, press Start again. Hmm, but if on title, one Start starts the game. The two-Start sequence is a safe way that works from either (if on title, first Start begins the game; the second Start during the 'WORLD 1-1' card... might pause? risky).\n\nActually, at reset the game is on the title. Pressing Start once begins the game. The prompt's note: \"Start on the title begins a game, but Start during the attract demo only returns to the title, so press Start, wait a second, press Start again.\" This means: if it's the attract demo, first Start returns to title, then second Start begins. If on title, first Start begins. So the two-Start sequence works if between the two the game goes: title -> (Start) -> game card -> ... The second Start 60 frames later might pause or be ignored during the card/level start. Risky per the MaxRightXSpdData note: \"the level had a leftover pause flag $0776=1 from an earlier extra Start\".\n\nSafest: after reset, press Start once and wait; check game mode. But that's more calls.\n\nActually, from reset the game is on the title (mapping: title scene reach = power-on). So one Start begins. Let me do [{start,6},{},120},{right,180}]. Then pause and check $0770=1 and a Goomba.\n\nHmm, but sometimes after reset it's already in the attract demo if we wait. reset immediately gives title.\n\nLet me do reset_emulator then play_input [{start,6},{},120},{right,180}].\n\nThen pause + list_sprites + screenshot. If no Goomba, hold right more.\n\nAlso clear pause flag just in case: not needed.\n\nLet me execute reset then play."}
