{"type":"text","text":"## Done. Enemy metasprite tile table found and proven\n\n**Table:** The PRG ROM enemy-metasprite tile-id list — records of **6 sprite-tile ids in OAM draw order** (row-major: top row left,right, then each lower row; `$FC` = blank top-row cell of a 16×24 form).\n\n**Goomba entry:** prgRom **`0x6792`–`0x6797` = `FC FC 70 71 72 73`** ($70/$71 upper body, $72/$73 feet; the `FC FC` is the blank top row).\n- Search hit: `70 71 72 73` is unique at `0x6794`; `FC FC 70 71 72 73` is unique at `0x6792`. The record sits on the 6-byte boundary of the tile-list block (base `0x673E`, entry 14), and it matches live OAM exactly (Goomba = OAM 52–57, palette 7, drawn `FC FC 70 71 72 73` upright / `FC FC 71 70 73 72` flipped).\n\n**Proof (persist-edit flow):** under hack **eval-sheet2-d**, `write_memory prgRom 0x6794` `$70 → $4F` (reason: replace the Goomba metasprite tile with Mario's body tile) — ledger seq 1, `persistent: true`. `reset_emulator`, replayed Start/Start to World 1-1, held Right until the first Goomba spawned (`$000F`=1). `list_sprites` then returned the Goomba as **`FC FC 71 4F 73 72`** (tile 79 instead of 112), and the paused screenshot shows the enemy with the changed cell. `undo_edit seq 1` restored `$70`.\n\n**Recorded:** `record_mapping` note id/name **\"enemy sprite layout table\"** with what the bytes are, the Goomba entry, the proof, and `rom_origins` prgRom **`0x673E` length `0x90`** (the bounded tile-list block `0x673E`–`0x67CD`; `0x67CE` starts a different structure, and the Goomba record is the 6 bytes at `0x6792`).\n\n**Finished:** `promote_mappings` (1 discovery promoted), then `use_hack default` — the active hack is back to `default`, and the eval hack's ledger is empty (edit undone)."}
